# Base change of the full divisor-expansion field equals L(j,j_M)

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange_adjoin_pair`
(`c2e0ccae-2e37-5fcb-85d3-6ec8e18edfe0`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `eeb9d044-5d89-5b95-8cc2-178a7f9f217b`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure and let $M$ be a nonzero natural
number. Assume `FunctionFieldGeneration M`, i.e. for every nonzero divisor $d$ of $M$ the series $q
\mapsto$ `qExpand ℚ d jq` (the Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ obtained from `jq` by the
substitution $q \mapsto q^{d}$, formally the rescaling of the Hahn-series support by multiplication
by $d$) lies in the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by `jq` and
`qExpand ℚ M jq`. Then the base change to $L$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull M`, namely the
intermediate field of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to
L$ of the subfield $\mathbb{Q}(\{\,$`qExpand ℚ d jq` $: d \mid M,\ d \neq 0\})$ of
$\mathbb{Q}((q))$, coincides with the intermediate field of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the two
elements `jqModC L` $= q^{-1}\cdot$ (image in $L$ of the integral power series
$E_4^{3}\cdot$`dedekindEtaUnitInv`), the $q$-expansion of $j$ with coefficients in $L$, and `jqNModC
L M` $=$ `qExpand L M (jqModC L)`, its substitution $q \mapsto q^{M}$.

This is the statement that the function field of $X_0(M)$ over a field $L$ of characteristic zero,
modelled as a subfield of $L((q))$ spanned by all divisor expansions $j(q^{d})$ with $d \mid M$, is
generated by the two functions $j(q)$ and $j(q^{M})$, once generation is known over $\mathbb{Q}$. It
supplies the two-generator description of the base-changed function field used throughout the later
analysis of places, nodes and specialisations of the $q$-expansion model of $X_0(M)$.

